<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Retail Inventory &amp; Store Performance — Ops Dashboard</title>
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/Chart.js/4.4.4/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg: #16181c;
    --panel: #1e2126;
    --panel-border: #2c3037;
    --ink: #eae7e0;
    --ink-dim: #9a9da3;
    --ink-dim2: #8b8e94;
    --amber: #ff7a1a;
    --amber-dim: #cc6414;
    --ok: #4caf7d;
    --warn: #e0473e;
    --grid: #2a2e34;
    --mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace;
    --sans: 'Inter', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  }
  @font-face{ font-family:'Inter'; src: local('Inter'); }
  *{ box-sizing: border-box; }
  html,body{
    margin:0; padding:0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  body{ padding: 28px 32px 60px; }

  .top-bar{
    display:flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-border); padding-bottom: 18px; margin-bottom: 22px;
    flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px;
  }
  .top-bar h1{
    font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: 0.2px;
  }
  .top-bar .sub{ color: var(--ink-dim2); font-size: 13px; }
  .badge-row{ display:flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .badge{
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-dim2);
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-border); padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .badge b{ color: var(--amber); font-weight: 600; }

  .kpi-strip{
    display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 1px;
    background: var(--panel-border); border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    margin-bottom: 22px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .kpi{ background: var(--panel); padding: 16px 18px; }
  .kpi .label{ font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-dim2); text-transform: none; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .kpi .value{ font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  .kpi .value.amber{ color: var(--amber); }
  .kpi .value.warn{ color: var(--warn); }
  .kpi .foot{ font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-dim2); margin-top: 4px; }

  .grid{
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .grid.thirds{ grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; }
  .panel{
    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--panel-border); border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .panel h2{
    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 2px; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .panel .desc{ font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-dim2); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .chart-wrap{ position: relative; height: 260px; }
  .chart-wrap.tall{ height: 320px; }

  table{ width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.5px; }
  thead th{
    text-align: left; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-dim2); font-size: 11px;
    padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
  }
  tbody td{ padding: 7px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #24272c; color: var(--ink); }
  tbody tr:last-child td{ border-bottom: none; }
  td.num, th.num{ font-family: var(--mono); text-align: right; }
  .pill{
    display:inline-block; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 3px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px;
  }
  .pill.risk-high{ background: rgba(224,71,62,0.15); color: #ff8b83; }
  .pill.risk-med{ background: rgba(255,122,26,0.15); color: var(--amber); }

  .footer-note{
    font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-dim2); margin-top: 26px; line-height: 1.6;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--panel-border); padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .footer-note b{ color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 900px){
    .grid, .grid.thirds{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .kpi-strip{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="top-bar">
    <div>
      <h1>Retail Inventory &amp; Store Performance</h1>
      <div class="sub">Multi-format retail network &middot; sales, inventory, and replenishment analytics</div>
    </div>
    <div class="badge-row">
      <div class="badge">STORES <b id="b-stores">--</b></div>
      <div class="badge">SKUs <b id="b-skus">--</b></div>
      <div class="badge">RANGE <b id="b-range">--</b></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kpi-strip">
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">Net revenue</div>
      <div class="value" id="k-revenue">--</div>
      <div class="foot">18-month total, net of promo discount</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">Units sold</div>
      <div class="value" id="k-units">--</div>
      <div class="foot">across all stores &amp; SKUs</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">Stockout rate</div>
      <div class="value warn" id="k-stockout">--</div>
      <div class="foot">% of item-days demand exceeded stock</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">Avg. inventory turnover</div>
      <div class="value amber" id="k-turnover">--</div>
      <div class="foot">annualized, COGS / avg inventory value</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">Days of supply</div>
      <div class="value" id="k-dos">--</div>
      <div class="foot">network average, on-hand vs. daily COGS</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Monthly net revenue — actual vs. 3-month forecast</h2>
      <div class="desc">Trailing 3-month moving average projected forward using recent trend slope</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall"><canvas id="chartRevenue"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Revenue by region &amp; store format</h2>
      <div class="desc">Where format mix drives (or drags on) regional performance</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall"><canvas id="chartRegion"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid thirds">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Stockout rate by category</h2>
      <div class="desc">% of item-days where demand outpaced on-hand stock</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartStockout"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Inventory turnover by category</h2>
      <div class="desc">Annualized COGS / avg. inventory value — lower ties up more cash</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartTurnover"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Top store performance</h2>
      <div class="desc">Highest net revenue, 18-month total</div>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Store</th><th>Region</th><th>Format</th><th class="num">Revenue</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="tbl-stores"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <h2>Reorder point recommendations — highest stockout-risk SKUs</h2>
    <div class="desc">Safety-stock model: ROP = (avg daily demand &times; lead time) + 1.65&sigma;&radic;(lead time) for a ~95% service level, 4-day supplier lead time</div>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Category</th><th class="num">Stockout rate</th><th class="num">Recommended ROP (units)</th><th class="num">Safety stock (units)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="tbl-risk"></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-note">
    <b>Methodology.</b> Data is a synthetic 18-month, 25-store, 38-SKU dataset built to mirror the operational shape of a general-merchandise / hardline retail network (SQL schema, generation script, and full query set included in the project repo). Metrics computed in SQL (SQLite) and Python (pandas); this dashboard renders the resulting summary. Reorder-point recommendations use a standard safety-stock formula and a 3&ndash;6 day simulated supplier lead time.
  </div>

